!Sample_source_name_ch1 = actue myeloid luekemia
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: MOLM-13 cell expressing SIK3T142Q
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: 2 hr treatment of 0.1% DMSO
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Cells were lentivirally infected with sgRNA for knockout, or treated with DMSO or 100 nM HG-9-91-01 for 2 hrs
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Cells were cultured in RPMI with 10% FBS and penicillin/streptomycin.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = polyA RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Total RNA was extracted using TRIzol following the manufacture's protocol
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA-seq library was prepared using Illumina TruSeq sample prep kit v2 according to the manufacture's protocol. Briefly, polyA RNA was selected and fragmented enzymatically. First strand of cDNA was synthesized using Super Script II reverse transcriptase, and then second strand was synthesized. Double-stranded cDNA was end-repaired, 3'-adenylated, ligated with indexed adaptor, and then PCR-amplified.
!Sample_description = RNAseq_MOLM13_emptyTQ_HG.txt
!Sample_data_processing = Sequencing reads were mapped into reference human genome hg19 using TopHat2
!Sample_data_processing = Differentially expressed genes were analyzed using a Cufflinks tool, Cuffdiff, by masking structural RNAs
!Sample_data_processing = normalized to total mapped reads
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg19
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: txt, normalized RPKM
